A mid-edit terragrunt.hcl and a module .tf file each end in a stray `@`
line after otherwise valid blocks: exactly one file-level GRT100 per broken
file, at the `@`. A reference into the unit sourcing the broken module is
silent (surface unknown), and a genuine missing output between two healthy
units is still reported.
-- live/midedit/terragrunt.hcl --
dependency "x" {
  config_path = "../ok_b"
}
@
-- modules/broken/main.tf --
output "ok" {
  value = 1
}
@
-- live/uses_broken/terragrunt.hcl --
terraform {
  source = "../../modules/broken"
}
-- live/dependant/terragrunt.hcl --
dependency "b" {
  config_path = "../uses_broken"
}

inputs = {
  v = dependency.b.outputs.not_declared
}
-- live/ok_b/terragrunt.hcl --
inputs = {}
-- live/ok_b/main.tf --
output "value" {
  value = "b"
}
-- live/ok_a/terragrunt.hcl --
dependency "b" {
  config_path = "../ok_b"
}

inputs = {
  good = dependency.b.outputs.value
  bad  = dependency.b.outputs.valeu
}
-- _golden/exit --
1
-- _golden/want --
# GRT100: one per broken file (hclconv.FirstSyntaxError), file-level so no
# unit, at the `@` on line 4 column 1.
GRT100 error live/midedit/terragrunt.hcl:4:1 -
GRT100 error modules/broken/main.tf:4:1 -
# live/ok_a/terragrunt.hcl line 7: "  bad  = " is 9 bytes.
GRT001 error live/ok_a/terragrunt.hcl:7:10 live/ok_a
